        "original_id": "4b2423c2-e062-5397-8d02-a020cef95eae",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Projects: Cascade Locks and Canal, Oregon Portage Railroad\n- Places: Columbia River, Oregon, Washington, Palm Beach County, Florida, Lake Worth Lagoon, Tanner Creek, Bonneville Dam\n\nFacts:\n- The Cascade Locks and Canal was a navigation project on the Columbia River between the U.S. states of Oregon and Washington, and it was completed in 1896.\n- During the later years of the Oregon Portage Railroad's operation, the Cascade Locks were under construction.\n- The Oregon Portage Railroad ran from Tanner Creek, near where Bonneville Dam was later built, to the Cascade Locks.\n- Lake Worth Lagoon is a lagoon located in Palm Beach County, Florida.",
